    "notes": "Four parts (Violin I, Violin II, Viola, Violoncello), one staff each, 8 bars of 4/4 in D major, 2 systems.  The viola reads alto clef, changes to treble on beat 3 of bar 3 and back to alto at the system start of bar 5 (courtesy clef at the end of system 1).  The cello changes bass -> tenor (bar 2) -> treble (bar 3 beat 2) -> tenor (bar 4 beat 3) -> bass (bar 6) -> tenor (bar 7 beat 3) -> bass (bar 8).  The D-major key signature (F#, C#) is drawn at different heights in alto and tenor clef; it must still give F# and C# in every octave."
  },
